                        "sense_id": "0b050182-a1f7-35d4-91f5-c0106248ad5d",
                        "entry_id": "3de52cd6-de5a-34d9-b618-b9ce648c8cbb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or quality of being fatherless (not having a (living) father)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5d41d16-3f29-471a-8a2f-88be80552c56",
                                "sense_id": "0b050182-a1f7-35d4-91f5-c0106248ad5d",
                                "text": "Speaking about the epidemic of fatherlessness in black families, Mr. Cosby imagined a young fatherless child thinking: “Somewhere in my life a person called my father has not shown up, and I feel very sad about this because I don’t know if I’m ugly — I don’t know what the reason is.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f76debb8-9f5e-4d82-8822-1defec2e0c5f",
                                "sense_id": "0b050182-a1f7-35d4-91f5-c0106248ad5d",
                                "text": "Obama did not respond to his fatherlessness or his racial predicament with anger and rage, but as questions for investigation, conversation and synthesis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b43bcb3b-886c-4f18-9d6a-a847a8142796",
                                "sense_id": "0b050182-a1f7-35d4-91f5-c0106248ad5d",
                                "text": "His themes have also been sounded by the comedian Bill Cosby, who has stirred debate among black Americans by bluntly speaking about an epidemic of fatherlessness in African-American families while suggesting that some blacks use racism as a crutch to explain the lack of economic progress."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
